{"type":"standard","title":"Pia Dandiya","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Pia Dandiya</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q136163054","titles":{"canonical":"Pia_Dandiya","normalized":"Pia Dandiya","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Pia Dandiya</span></span>"},"pageid":81007553,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Pia_Dandiya_WHF_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":125,"height":156},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Pia_Dandiya_WHF_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":125,"height":156},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1383719790","tid":"515fca88-d83e-11f1-9f94-9f3eff85fe80","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:55:59Z","description":"American politician","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pia_Dandiya","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pia_Dandiya?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pia_Dandiya?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Pia_Dandiya"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pia_Dandiya","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Pia_Dandiya","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pia_Dandiya?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Pia_Dandiya"}},"extract":"Pia Dandiya is an American educator, former technology executive, and politician who is the United States representative-elect from Florida's 22nd congressional district. A former high school principal and White House Fellow, she later led public-sector initiatives at Apple Inc. She was the Democratic nominee for Florida's 22nd congressional district in the 2026 election, defeating Republican nominee Casey Askar.","extract_html":"<p><b>Pia Dandiya</b> is an American educator, former technology executive, and politician who is the United States representative-elect from Florida's 22nd congressional district. A former high school principal and White House Fellow, she later led public-sector initiatives at Apple Inc. She was the Democratic nominee for Florida's 22nd congressional district in the 2026 election, defeating Republican nominee Casey Askar.</p>"}